# BuildKit reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to the context's .dockerignore, so this
# file -- not the root .dockerignore -- governs what the OSS Scanner build sees. The root one is
# written for the published node image and hides .github, which the auditing agent wants.
#
# If a builder ever ignores this file, the root .dockerignore applies instead: that is a smaller
# context, not a broken build, so the degradation is safe.

# The scanner's own pipeline copies .git back into /src after the build, so paying to send a large
# history through the build context here would be wasted.
.git

# Local developer state. Absent from the scanner's fresh clone; excluded so a build run from a
# working tree matches what the scanner sees.
.gradle
.gradle-test
.idea
.vscode
.claude
build
rskj-core/build
logs
**/.sonar
